# X-Plane Plugin Support

LinuxTrack builds two X-Plane plugins when the SDK is present at configure time:

- **xlinuxtrack.so** — legacy plugin for X-Plane 8.x and 9.x
- **xlinuxtrack9.so** — current plugin for X-Plane 9.x and newer

## X-Plane SDK (required to build)

1. **Download**: [X-Plane plugin SDK downloads](https://developer.x-plane.com/sdk/plugin-sdk-downloads/) — current releases are **ZIP** archives (e.g. `XPSDK430.zip`; the version in the filename may change).
2. **Extract**: Archives contain `SDK/CHeaders/` (not `.tar.gz`). See [docs/readme/x-plane-sdk.md](../../readme/x-plane-sdk.md) for full steps.
3. **Configure**: `-DENABLE_XPLANE=ON -DXPLANE_SDK_PATH=/opt/xplane-sdk/CHeaders` (CMake default search path is `/opt/xplane-sdk/CHeaders`).

## Usage

After installation, enable the plugin in X-Plane’s plugin manager for head tracking support.
